<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis steady, sales moderate.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis steady, sales moderate.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal basis offers were mostly unchanged with buyers continuing to seek product for prompt shipment, dealers said.</p>
<p>The soymeal basis offer at Decatur, Ill., rose $1.00 to $13.00 per ton over CBOT July futures. Offers at other locations were unchanged, but dealers said values were firm because many processors have had to raise soybean basis bids.</p>
<p>Several dealers expect Thursday's National Oilseed Processors Association weekly crush to come out as unchanged to slightly lower from the previous week's crush of 25.632 million bushels.  </p>
